   Context Sensitive Help
   ======================
       Artisoft Exchange on-line Help is now context sensitive. From any
       window or dialog box, press F1 to get instant Help. Once you're in
       the Help window, you can use the jump, browse and search features
       to see other Help topics.

   Logging In to Mail
   ==================
       When you're not using LANtastic accounts for Artisoft Exchange,
       mail users must enter a username and password to log in to their
       mail account. For information on what to type in the log-in fields,
       press F1 when the log-in screen is visible.

       When you're already logged in to Artisoft Exchange Mail, you don't
       need to type in a password (if one is set) to enter Artisoft
       Exchange Scheduler.  The same rule applies if you're logged into
       Artisoft Exchange Scheduler and want to use Artisoft Exchange Mail.

       Important!  In order to use Artisoft Exchange, you must be logged
                   in to the Post Office computer.

     Log-In Error Messages
     ---------------------
       Some of the error messages described in the Artisoft Exchange
       User's Manual have changed slightly.  The steps for correcting
       these errors remain as described in the manual.

       One message has changed completely. The old message which read:

              "Personal directory path is invalid or read only"

       now appears as follows:

              "Local Temp Directory Path is Invalid."

       Other common error messages are described below.

       Artisoft Exchange Mail is not in server mode
         You can't choose the Post Office icon or run MTAEXEC on a
         computer running in Client mode. Follow the steps for setting up
         the Server later in this file, then choose the Post Office icon,
         or run MTAEXEC.

       Message Store Directory Path is Invalid
         You may get this message if you're using a mail Server. If you
         see this message, make sure you're logged into the server
         computer. See your LANtastic manuals for information on logging
         in to servers. If this doesn't correct the problem, follow the
         instructions given for correcting this error in your Artisoft
         Exchange User's Manual.

   Searching for Objects
   =====================
       When you search for an object, you can use wildcard characters
       such as ? or *. To search for one of these characters, precede
       it with a backslash. For example, if you want to search for a
       wildcard account, you could type /* in the search box.

       Note: Artisoft Exchange Mail will search for an exact match of what
             you type in a Search box, unless you place an asterisk (*)
             at the beginning and end of the search string.

       To search for a message based on what's in its Subject box, use
       the extended search criteria features described under "Searching
       for Objects" in your Artisoft Exchange User's Manual.

   Printing through the Fax Printer Driver
   =======================================
       When you install Artisoft Exchange, a fax printer driver
       (ARTFAX.DRV) is copied into your WINDOWS\SYSTEM directory.  New
       instructions for sending a fax appear below. Instructions can also
       be found in "Printing through the Fax Printer Driver" in the How Do
       I? section of on-line Help for Artisoft Exchange Mail.

     Sending a Fax through Artisoft Exchange Mail
     --------------------------------------------
         1. Create a new message, or open an existing one.

         2. Choose Print from the Message menu. The Print Setup window
            appears.

         3. In the Print Setup window, choose Specific Printers. Choose
            the arrow to the right of the Specific Printers box to pull
            down a list of available printer drivers.

         4. Select Artisoft Fax Printer Driver.

         5. Choose OK to send the fax.

     Sending a Fax from Other Windows Applications
     ---------------------------------------------
       ARTFAX.DRV is a Windows printer driver. You can use it from
       other Windows applications, such as Microsoft Word. The steps below
       assume that you've selected the fax printer driver to be the
       default printer driver for your computer. See your Windows
       documentation for instructions.

       If you have a CAS-compatible fax modem installed on your computer:

         1. From the application, choose Print. The Options window
            appears.

         2. In the Options box in the upper left, choose either Local or
            Mail.

              - If you choose Local, the fax is sent directly through the
                fax modem on your computer.

                   - If desired, fill in the To and Phone boxes in the
                     Local Send Information box.  The information in the
                     From and Logo file boxes was set up when you
                     installed the CAS manager software. The subject
                     contains the application and the name of the file.

                   - Choose OK to send the fax.

              - If you choose Mail, the fax will be attached to an
                Artisoft Exchange Mail message, which you can send to a
                fax address or other address.

                   - Choose OK to bring up the Artisoft Exchange Mail
                     log-in screen.

                   - Follow the instructions in your Artisoft Exchange
                     User's Manual for addressing and sending a message.
                     To send the message as a fax, send it to a fax
                     address.

       If you have a fax modem installed on the mail Server computer:

         1. From the application, choose Print.

         2. The printer output is printed to a file, which is then
            attached to an Artisoft Exchange Mail message. (Before you see
            the message with the print file attached, you may have to log
            in to Artisoft Exchange Mail.)

         3. Follow the instructions in your Artisoft Exchange User's
            Manual for addressing and sending a message.  To fax the
            message, send the message to a fax address.

       To use a fax modem installed on the mail Server computer, the mail
       administrator must have set up a Fax Gateway on the server.

       Note: You may not use the fax printer driver across the network; it
             must be located in the Windows directory on the local
             computer.

   Memory and Configuration Requirements
   =====================================
       The recommended minimum configuration for a computer running
       Artisoft Exchange is a 386SX or faster processor with 4MB of RAM.

   Automatically Setting Up Gateways and the Server
   ================================================
       For your convenience, the procedure for setting up a dedicated mail
       server has been improved. The Gateways and Server are
       automatically set up during the installation on the Post Office
       computer, but they're disabled. To use Server-based mail, and to
       use the pre-configured Gateways, follow these steps.

         1. Log in with the username SYSTEM.

         2. Open the User Accounts folder.

         3. Pull down the Administration menu and choose Post Office Mode.
            The Server/Client window appears.

         4. Check the Server button, then choose OK.

        All the Gateways and the Server are set up, but only the Server is
        automatically enabled. The Gateways that are set up are:

           Fax Gateway
           Pager Gateway
           Text Pager Gateway
           LANtastic Mail Gateway

        To use a Gateway you must turn it on by following the steps in the
        next few sections. You may also need to change the default
        settings to match your modem or fax board.

     Activating the Fax Gateway
     --------------------------
         1. Make sure you have a compatible fax modem (fax board)
            installed on the mail server. See the Artisoft Exchange User's
            Manual for more information about supported fax modems.

         2. Log in with the username SYSTEM.

         3. Open Gateway Folders.

         4. Open the folder with the same name as the main Post Office.
            (This is the same name you entered during the installation.)

         5. Open the MTA Events folder.

         6. Open the MTA CAS Fax object.

         7. In the box titled Interval (seconds), enter a positive time
            interval, such as 60 for one minute. See your Artisoft
            Exchange User's Manual for a complete description of the
            settings in this window.

         8. If desired, choose the Options button to change the default
            settings. See your Artisoft Exchange User's Manual for a
            complete description of the settings in this window.

       Note: In the Fax Gateway Information window, which appears when you
             choose the Options button, the name of the first input field
             has changed. Administrator's Address appears in the manual,
             while the screen now says Administrator's Account. Enter the
             account name of the person who'll be receiving and
             distributing incoming faxes.

         9. Choose Save from the MTA menu.

     Activating the Pager Gateways
     -----------------------------
         1. Make sure you have a compatible modem installed on COM2
            on the mail server. To use the Digital Pager, the modem
            phone line must be a Touchtone phone line.

         2. Log in with the username SYSTEM.

         3. Open Gateway Folders.

         4. Open the folder with the same name as the main Post Office.
            (This is the same name you entered during the installation.)

         5. Open the MTA Events folder.

         6. Open the MTA Digital Pager object to set up the Digital
            Pager. Open the MTA Alpha Pager object to set up the
            Text Pager.

         7. In the box titled Interval (seconds), enter a positive time
            interval, such as 60 for one minute. See your Artisoft
            Exchange User's Manual for a complete description of the
            settings in this window.

         8. If desired, choose the Options button to change the default
            settings, such as baud rate, data bits and init strings.  See
            your Artisoft Exchange User's Manual for a complete
            description of the settings in this window.

         9. Choose Save from the MTA menu.

     Activating the LANtastic Mail Gateway
     -------------------------------------
         1. Log in with the username SYSTEM.

         2. Open Gateway Folders.

         3. Open the folder with the same name as the main Post Office.
            (This is the name you entered during the installation.)

         4. Open the MTA Events folder.

         5. Open the MTA LANtastic Mail object.

         6. In the box titled Interval (seconds), enter a positive time
            interval, such as 60 for one minute. See your Artisoft
            Exchange User's Manual for a complete description of the
            settings in this window.

         7. Choose Save from the MTA menu.

         8. Close the MTA Events window.  Close the main Post Office
            window to return to the Gateway Folders window.

         9. Open the LANtastic Mail folder.

        10. Open the MTA Events folder.

        11. Open the LANtastic Queue Object.

        12. Enter the name of the LANtastic mail server in the Source
            Server box.

        13. Choose Save from the Queue menu.

       See the Artisoft Exchange User's Manual for additional setup
       options.

   Setting Up a Network Post Office to Post Office Gateway
   =======================================================
       The path listed under Remote Message Store Directory is incorrect
       as it appears in the Artisoft Exchange User's Manual. The following
       path:

              \\server\c-drive\amail\

       should read:

              \\SERVER\C-DRIVE\LANTASTI\AMAIL

       The path is correct as it appears in the on-line Help.

   Setting Up the LANtastic Queue Gateway
   ======================================
       Some additional information for setting up a LANtastic Queue
       Gateway has been added to the "LANtastic Queue Gateway" topic in
       the Administration section of on-line Help for Artisoft Exchange
       Mail. (This information is not in the Artisoft Exchange
       User's Manual.)

  Message Logging for Gateways
  ============================
       Gateway accounts don't have a Sent folder. When a message is sent
       through a Gateway, a copy of the Message is NOT saved in the
       Gateway account. If the client sending the message has a Sent
       folder, a copy of the message will be stored there.

   Using the Log File Browser
   ==========================
       This feature allows the mail administrator to easily view error
       messages and other information sent to the log file by Artisoft
       Exchange Mail. For complete information on reading a log file, see
       "Using the Log File Browser" in the Administration section of
       on-line Help.

   Setting Up the CAS Manager
   ==========================
       To use Artisoft Exchange's fax capabilities, you must have a CAS
       manager running on your computer.  See your CAS manager
       documentation for information on loading the CAS manager.

   Using Intel's FAXPOP.EXE
   ========================
       If you're using Intel's FAXPOP.EXE, make sure the FAXPOP
       application loads after LANtastic's REDIR.EXE program.  Loading
       FAXPOP before REDIR.EXE will cause your computer to lock up.

   Running a DOS Server
   ====================
       You don't have to run Windows on the Artisoft Exchange server.
       To use a DOS-only server:

          - Install the Post Office on the server.  To perform a Windows
            installation through DOS, use the /DOS/WIN switch described in
            the installation chapters in the LANtastic Installation and
            Management Guide.

          - From a client computer, log into SYSTEM and set up the
            Gateways. Steps for setting up the Gateways appear earlier in
            this file.

          - Change to the directory containing the Artisoft Exchange
            program files and type MTAEXEC <Enter> at the DOS prompt. For
            example, if you installed to the default directory, type:

              CD C:\LANTASTI\AMAILPRG <Enter>
              MTAEXEC <Enter>

       Note: You may not run MTAEXEC with LANtastic's ALONE program.

       To administer a DOS-only Artisoft Exchange server, log in to the
       System account from any Artisoft Exchange client in the network.

   Using the Admin Account
   =======================
       When you install the Post Office on a computer, an account called
       Admin is created by default. This is an account used for storing
       incoming faxes and storing special error notices for the mail
       administrator.

       To log in to the Admin account, type ADMIN in the Username box when
       you log in. The first time you log in you won't need to enter a
       password. Choose OK or press Enter.

       When an MTA or Gateway is removed from the mail server, a message
       is sent to the Admin account describing the error. Some MHS-based
       mail systems may send error messages and directory updates to the
       Admin account.

       To read and delete these messages, log in to the Admin account as
       described above, then open the In folder. Even if you don't
       regularly use the Admin account, you may want to log in
       periodically to delete accumulated messages. The mail administrator
       may want to set up a filter to forward all mail sent to the Admin
       account to her own account.

   Using SHARE with Artisoft Exchange
   ==================================
       For the Post Office computer ONLY, the File Name Spaces setting for
       SHARE must be at least 10K.  Instructions for changing the File
       Name Spaces setting for LANtastic's SHARE program appear below.  If
       you are using DOS SHARE, see your DOS manual.

         1. At the DOS prompt type NET_MGR <Enter>

         2. Select Server Startup Parameters <Enter>.

         3. Select Internal SHARE <Enter>.

         4. Select Name Space <Enter>.

         5. Type 10000 <Enter>.

         6. Press Esc at each screen to return to the DOS prompt.

   Scheduling Global Appointments
   ==============================
       The administrator can schedule global appointments, such as
       national holidays and organization-wide meetings, for every
       Artisoft Exchange Scheduler account.

       Global appointments appear in your daily schedule with a globe
       symbol on the appointment line. Global recurring appointments
       appear in blue on the monthly calendar and daily schedule, just as
       personal recurring appointments do. Non-recurring (one-time) global
       appointments appear in purple.

       The administrator creates and modifies global appointments by
       logging into the scheduler as the SYSTEM account. Every new
       appointment the administrator creates while logged into the System
       account will be a global appointment.  The same steps for creating
       and editing personal and recurring appointments are used for global
       appointments. When the administrator chooses the New Appointment
       button, the New Appointment dialog box that appears is identical to
       the dialog box that would appear for creating a new personal
       appointment.  When the Recurring Appointment button is selected,
       the new appointments created will be global recurring appointments.

       Note: One type of appointment the system administrator can create
             through the System account won't schedule every account in
             the organization: the group appointment. Only the
             participants the system administrator selects will be
             included in the group appointment.

       To view global appointments, choose a date on your calendar that
       contains a global appointment, then choose the appointment line
       that has a globe symbol. If it's a one-time appointment, the Global
       Appointment window appears, showing all information about the
       appointment. If it's a global recurring appointment, the Recurring
       Appointment window appears. Choose OK to close either of these
       windows.
